2. Process requirement lib [1..3] - try lib=3 first
3. Process lib=3's requirement core [3..3] - assign core=3
4. Process requirement util [3..3] - assign util=3
5. Process util=3's requirement core [1..1] - but core=3 is already assigned, which violates this requirement
6. Backtrack to try lib=2
7. Process lib=2's requirement core [1..2] - assign core=2
8. Process requirement util [3..3] - assign util=3
9. Process util=3's requirement core [1..1] - but core=2 is already assigned, which violates this requirement
10. Backtrack to try lib=1
11. Process requirement util [3..3] - assign util=3
12. Process util=3's requirement core [1..1] - assign core=1
13. All requirements satisfied

For Universe B, the resolution should fail because x requires core [1..1] and y requires core [2..2], which is impossible to satisfy simultaneously.

